### 3. The Alternative Full Setup Wizard (reached via the setup path)

This is a longer, more structured alternative to the quick ModeSelect flow. It's accessible from the Dashboard's "Setup & Hardware" button or by manually navigating to the sub-routes. Steps:

**`/setup/device-check`** — System check screen
- Four parallel `invoke()` calls for RAM, disk, CPU, and internet
- Each check gets a green/amber/red status badge
- Auto-advances to `/setup/model-select` on pass/warn

**`/setup/model-select`** — AI Model download
- Three model choices: `llama3.2:3b` (2 GB, fast), `llama3.2:8b` (5 GB, smarter), `llama3.1:70b` (40 GB, requires 64 GB RAM)
- Download is a real Tauri-invoked operation with SHA-256 hash verification; progress comes back via Tauri events
- Saves `selected_model` to localStorage, navigates to `/setup/agent-select`

**`/setup/agent-select`** — Agent selection
- Full filterable grid of all 55+ agents from the registry
- Top search bar + horizontal category pill filter (Sales, Support, Operations, Marketing, Finance, HR, Productivity, Legal, Coding, Research, Logistics)
- Each card shows: category icon, agent name, 2-line description, up to 3 integration icons, category label
- Selection toggled by clicking; selected state shows a brand-colored border + check badge
- A sticky footer counts selected agents and the "Activate N agents →" button is disabled until at least one is chosen
- On confirm: creates agent objects, writes to `localStorage.agentiq_agents` and `selected_agents`, adds to Zustand store, navigates to `/setup/integrations`

**`/setup/integrations`** — Animated activation sequence
- Reads `selected_agents` from localStorage, hydrates each from the registry
- Builds a flat list of `TaskStep` items: for each agent → load skills → apply instructions → activate each integration → verify workspace; plus a first "Securing workspace" step and a final "Finalizing" step
- Steps auto-advance every 320ms (purely visual / simulated — no real OAuth happens here)
- Right panel shows a "Team setup summary" sidebar with each agent's icon, name, skill count, and integration count
- A note says: "Services requiring account authorization will ask for consent only when an agent first needs them."
- "Continue" button appears when complete, navigates to `/setup/agent-config`

**`/setup/agent-config`** — Per-agent configuration
- Renders a dynamic form for each selected agent using react-hook-form + Zod schemas
- Dynamic field types: slider, toggle, select, text input, file upload, time-range picker
- Currently has full schemas for `research-general`, `code-assistant`, `email-marketer`; all others fall back to `research-general` schema
- Saves via `invoke('save_agent_configs')`, navigates to `/setup/voice-setup`

**`/setup/voice-setup`** — Voice configuration
- Configures local (Whisper/Coqui) vs cloud (Deepgram/ElevenLabs) voice I/O
- Saves `voice_config` to localStorage

**`/setup/launch`** — Final launch screen
- Reads all localStorage keys and builds a visual `SetupTimeline` checklist showing which setup phases were completed vs pending
- "Launch Your Team" button calls `invoke('start_orchestrator')`, waits 2 seconds for animation, sets `setup_complete=true`, navigates to `/?onboarding=true` (which lands at `/workspace`)

